*---------------------------------- 1 rty_arbno_extend_double_fires_cond_capture
* rty_arbno_extend_double_fires_cond_capture -- FALSIFICATION WITNESS (hq_C, s261)
* A deferred conditional capture ( . *FN() ) whose captured sub-pattern contains an
* ARBNO that EXTENDS after the capture's first success fires its action TWICE:
* once at the premature shorter extent, once at the final extent.
* Oracle prints P P P A ; the defect prints P P A P A (one extra A).
* Minimal: the INNER capture is NOT required -- ARBNO alone, uncaptured, is enough.
* Mechanism: bb_match_capture.cpp IR_MATCH_CAPTURE_COND appends the pend entry at
* alpha (add r12,24) and retracts it ONLY on the beta->omega concede path; an ARBNO
* extension re-enters alpha without ever conceding, so the first entry is never
* retracted and rt_dcap_pump replays it.  Same family as rung-arbno-selfloop.
        DEFINE('P()')                           :(P_end)
P       OUTPUT = 'P'
        P = .dm                                 :(NRETURN)
P_end
        DEFINE('A()')                           :(A_end)
A       OUTPUT = 'A'
        A = .dm                                 :(NRETURN)
A_end
        F = SPAN('0123456789') . *P()
        T = F ARBNO('*' F)
        X = T ARBNO('+' T . *A())
        C = POS(0) X RPOS(0)
        '1+2*3' C                               :S(y)F(n)
y       OUTPUT = 'ok'                           :(END)
n       OUTPUT = 'no'
END
*------------------------------------------------------ 2 rty_arbno_leftctx_cond
*  HQ's UNMEASURED PREDICTION (FINDING-2026-08-22-s256): the byte-identical defect at
*  lower_snobol4.c:1439-1442 (TT_CAPT_COND_ASGN, the . operator) should hang on the SAME
*  shape rty_arbno_leftctx_inline hangs on with $ -- this is the falsification witness,
*  minted by the curing seat per HQ LAW 17 before assuming the prediction is correct.
*  ⛔ CAPTURE STDOUT WITH A HARD timeout WHEN RUNNING THIS -- MAY NOT TERMINATE.
	&ANCHOR = 1
	subj = "this is a test ."
	subj (BREAK(' ') ARBNO(LEN(1))) . OUTPUT '.'
END
*---------------------------------------------------- 3 rty_arbno_leftctx_inline
*  RED, CHECKED IN RED (law 0d).  ***AN ARBNO PRECEDED BY ANOTHER ELEMENT NEVER RETRIES,
*  AND THE STATEMENT RUNS AWAY.***  Reduced from corpus/programs/csnobol4-suite/breakx's
*  second statement (BREAK(' ') ARBNO(LEN(1) BREAK(' '))).  BREAKX itself is CURED (s192,
*  rty-fail-inline-retry) -- this is a DIFFERENT, still-open defect: ARBNO's own retry
*  wiring, when ARBNO is NOT the leftmost element of its (...)$ group.  The oracle prints
*  each extension t/th/thi/this/... up to the literal; SCRIP prints "this" forever.
*  ⛔ CAPTURE STDOUT WITH A HARD timeout WHEN RUNNING THIS -- SCRIP DOES NOT TERMINATE.
	&ANCHOR = 1
	subj = "this is a test ."
	subj (BREAK(' ') ARBNO(LEN(1))) $ OUTPUT '.'
END
*---------------------------------------------------- 4 rty_arbno_leftctx_stored
*  RED, CHECKED IN RED (law 0d).  The IDENTICAL pattern stored in a variable first hangs
*  EXACTLY like the inline twin rty_arbno_leftctx_inline -- this rules out the inline-vs-
*  stored/blob dichotomy that explained the BAL/ARB family (s192): here BOTH roads are red,
*  so the defect is in ARBNO's own retry state, not in which road compiles the pattern.
*  ⛔ CAPTURE STDOUT WITH A HARD timeout WHEN RUNNING THIS -- SCRIP DOES NOT TERMINATE.
	&ANCHOR = 1
	subj = "this is a test ."
	p = BREAK(' ') ARBNO(LEN(1))
	subj p $ OUTPUT '.'
END
*-------------------------------------------------------- 5 rty_arbno_noleft_ctl
*  CONTROL, GREEN -- the ONE-INGREDIENT twin of rty_arbno_leftctx_inline with the leading
*  BREAK removed, so the ARBNO is the LEFTMOST element of its group.  Extends and
*  terminates correctly (t/th/thi/this/...).  Proves ARBNO's OWN retry is sound in
*  isolation -- the defect needs a left neighbour ahead of the ARBNO to appear.
	&ANCHOR = 1
	subj = "this is a test ."
	subj ARBNO(LEN(1)) $ OUTPUT '.'
END
*--------------------------------------------------------- 6 rty_break_nogen_ctl
*  CONTROL, GREEN -- BREAK alone (no ARBNO) is NOT a generator (unlike BREAKX): it proposes
*  one candidate, and on failure retreats without retrying.  Guards NO-PER-OP-FILTER: any
*  future cure for rty_arbno_leftctx_inline must not make plain BREAK start retrying too.
	&ANCHOR = 1
	subj = "this is a test ."
	subj BREAK(' ') $ OUTPUT '.'
END
*--------------------------------------------------------- 7 rty_deadlit_arb_ctl
*  CONTROL, GREEN, AND THE SHARPEST ONE -- the driver is a literal 'Z' that can NEVER match, so
*  it fails exactly as FAIL does, and the generator extends correctly (null/A/AB/ABC).  The
*  defect is therefore NOT 'an always-failing right element': it is the FAIL NODE ITSELF.
 'ABC' ? POS(0) ARB $ OUTPUT 'Z'
 OUTPUT = 'done'
END
*--------------------------------------------------------- 8 rty_fail_arb_inline
*  RED, CHECKED IN RED (law 0d).  Same defect one generator over: ARB $ OUTPUT FAIL fires once
*  (oracle enumerates null/A/AB/ABC).  Falls with rty_fail_bal_inline -- ONE class, two members,
*  which is why neither may be cured by an op-conditioned admission (NO-PER-OP-FILTER).
 'ABC' ? POS(0) ARB $ OUTPUT FAIL
 OUTPUT = 'done'
END
*--------------------------------------------------------- 9 rty_fail_bal_inline
*  RED, CHECKED IN RED (law 0d).  ***FAIL DOES NOT DRIVE GENERATOR RETRY, INLINE ROAD.***
*  The manual's own enumeration idiom: BAL is a generator that EXTENDS on retry, and the
*  FAIL element forces the scanner to re-drive it -- oracle prints A/AB/ABC.  SCRIP fires the
*  generator ONCE.  ⭐ THE STORED TWIN rty_fail_bal_stored_ctl IS GREEN: the blob road wires
*  this retreat correctly and the INLINE statement-graph road does not -- the OPPOSITE road
*  from the rty_fence_* family beside it.
 'ABC' ? POS(0) BAL $ OUTPUT FAIL
 OUTPUT = 'done'
END
*---------------------------------------------------- 10 rty_fail_bal_stored_ctl
*  CONTROL, GREEN -- the SAME pattern stored in a variable and matched through the compiled
*  PAT$n blob.  Prints A/AB/ABC correctly.  This is the one-token twin of rty_fail_bal_inline
*  and proves the defect is the INLINE road, not BAL and not FAIL semantics.
        p = BAL $ OUTPUT FAIL
        'ABC' ? POS(0) p
        OUTPUT = 'done'
END
*---------------------------------------------------------- 11 rty_fail_span_ctl
*  CONTROL, GREEN -- SPAN is NOT an extending generator, so firing once IS correct here.
*  Guards the cure: whatever fixes the reds must leave this printing 'ABC' exactly once.
 'ABC' ? POS(0) SPAN('ABC') $ OUTPUT FAIL
 OUTPUT = 'done'
END
*------------------------------------------------------ 12 rty_fence_arbno_defer
*  RED, CHECKED IN RED (law 0d).  The deferred reference *expr fails identically to the bare
*  reference -- the defect is in the stored pattern's own resume surface, not in the defer road.
        expr  = LEN(1) ARBNO(FENCE('+') LEN(1))
        '1+2+3' POS(0) *expr RPOS(0)                    :S(Y)F(N)
Y OUTPUT = 'match'                                      :(END)
N OUTPUT = 'nomatch'
END
*------------------------------------------------- 13 rty_fence_arbno_inline_ctl
*  CONTROL, GREEN -- the IDENTICAL pattern text written INLINE matches at every iteration count
*  tested (1..7).  The one-token twin of rty_fence_arbno_stored: stored-vs-inline is the whole
*  difference, which places this in the blob resume-surface family, not in FENCE semantics.
        '1+2+3' POS(0) LEN(1) ARBNO(FENCE('+') LEN(1)) RPOS(0)  :S(Y)F(N)
Y OUTPUT = 'match'                                              :(END)
N OUTPUT = 'nomatch'
END
*----------------------------------------------------- 14 rty_fence_arbno_stored
*  RED, CHECKED IN RED (law 0d).  ***A STORED PATTERN WHOSE ARBNO BODY BEGINS WITH FENCE(x)
*  FOLLOWED BY ANOTHER ELEMENT NEVER MATCHES.***  Reduced from crosscheck 145_pat_left_assoc_
*  via_arbno_fence (oracle 'first=1 last=5', SCRIP 'fail').  Capture and SPAN are NOT
*  ingredients -- both were ablated away.  Iteration count is NOT an ingredient either: the
*  1-iteration twin rty_fence_arbno_stored_1iter is equally red.
        expr  = LEN(1) ARBNO(FENCE('+') LEN(1))
        '1+2+3' POS(0) expr RPOS(0)                     :S(Y)F(N)
Y OUTPUT = 'match'                                      :(END)
N OUTPUT = 'nomatch'
END
*----------------------------------------------- 15 rty_fence_arbno_stored_1iter
*  RED, CHECKED IN RED (law 0d).  ONE iteration ('1+2') and still red -- kills the iteration-
*  count hypothesis outright.  ⛔ HQ nearly published that false hypothesis: rewriting the
*  witness to vary the count silently moved it to the INLINE road (all green), which is a
*  reminder that an ablation must change ONE thing and the road is a thing.
        expr  = LEN(1) ARBNO(FENCE('+') LEN(1))
        '1+2' POS(0) expr RPOS(0)                       :S(Y)F(N)
Y OUTPUT = 'match'                                      :(END)
N OUTPUT = 'nomatch'
END
*----------------------------------------------- 16 rty_fence_capdefer_both_segv
*  CURED s193 (row rty-fence-arbno-stored, FENCE1-DEPTH).  Was m3 SIGSEGV (rc=139) + m4 'fail' -- a MODE
*  DIVERGENCE as well as a wrong answer.  The shape of crosscheck 145 with a LITERAL subject.  The s192
*  header on this file named the mechanism and was right: the FENCE1 box stored/restored rsp through a
*  STATIC-DEPTH slot, the premise the lowerer itself records as violated inside an ARBNO body ("rsp
*  moves per iteration, Tier D").  What it could not yet say is WHERE the slot landed: at the deeper
*  iteration it resolved onto the blob head's saved-operand cell [rbp-24] (blob_head_bytes), which
*  IR_MATCH_DEFER reads as its pattern.  CURE: emit.cpp fence_frame_candidate admits ival==2, moving the
*  watermark into the activation frame.  ABLATION KEPT (all green, checked in beside this file):
*  capture+defer on ONE side only (rty_fence_capdefer_left_ctl, rty_fence_capdefer_right_ctl).
        num   = SPAN('0123456789')
        expr  = num . FIRST ARBNO(FENCE('+') num . LAST)
        '1+2+3' POS(0) expr RPOS(0)                     :S(Y)F(N)
Y OUTPUT = 'match'                                      :(END)
N OUTPUT = 'fail'
END
*------------------------------------------------ 17 rty_fence_capdefer_left_ctl
*  CONTROL, GREEN (s192).  capture+defer on element 0 ONLY -- the ARBNO body right of the FENCE is a bare
*  defer.  One token from rty_fence_capdefer_both_segv and it neither crashes nor mis-answers, which is
*  what makes the crash a BOTH-SIDES fact rather than a defer-in-a-fenced-body fact.
        num   = SPAN('0123456789')
        expr  = num . FIRST ARBNO(FENCE('+') num)
        '1+2+3' POS(0) expr RPOS(0)                     :S(Y)F(N)
Y OUTPUT = 'match'                                      :(END)
N OUTPUT = 'fail'
END
*----------------------------------------------- 18 rty_fence_capdefer_plainleft
*  CURED s193 (row rty-fence-arbno-stored, FENCE1-DEPTH).  Was the residual after s192 FENCE-RTAIL and
*  the minimal spelling of what still failed crosscheck 145.  The carrier was published CORRECTLY here
*  (SCRIP_RESUME_WHY=1: body_root_op=57 tier=1 f1r=0, identical to the GREEN right_ctl beside it), so
*  the defect was one box further in.  IR_MATCH_FENCE1 banked its watermark at a STATIC RSP offset
*  ('mov [rsp+176], rsp'), but a FENCE1 in an ARBNO body is re-entered one iteration DEEPER every time:
*  on iteration 2 that same +176 resolved to [rbp-24], the blob head's DTP cell (blob_head_bytes), and
*  IR_MATCH_DEFER then loaded the fence's own saved rsp as its pattern operand.  CURE: emit.cpp
*  fence_frame_candidate admits ival==2 (FENCE1-in-ARBNO, stamped lower_snobol4.c:1695), so the
*  watermark rides the activation-frame slot [rbp-80] that the R-4(f) SLICE 3 arm already provided.
        num   = SPAN('0123456789')
        expr  = LEN(1) ARBNO(FENCE('+') num . LAST)
        '1+2+3' POS(0) expr RPOS(0)                     :S(Y)F(N)
Y OUTPUT = 'match'                                      :(END)
N OUTPUT = 'fail'
END
*----------------------------------------------- 19 rty_fence_capdefer_right_ctl
*  CONTROL, GREEN (s192).  capture+defer inside the ARBNO body ONLY -- element 0 is a capture over a LEAF.
*  The other half of the ablation: this is the exact body the SEGV witness has, proving the body alone is
*  not the ingredient.  ⭐ It is also a CURE: red ('fail') before s192 FENCE-RTAIL, green after, both modes.
        num   = SPAN('0123456789')
        expr  = LEN(1) . FIRST ARBNO(FENCE('+') num . LAST)
        '1+2+3' POS(0) expr RPOS(0)                     :S(Y)F(N)
Y OUTPUT = 'match'                                      :(END)
N OUTPUT = 'fail'
END
*----------------------------------------------------- 20 rty_nofence_stored_ctl
*  CONTROL, GREEN -- the same STORED pattern with the FENCE removed.  Proves the stored road
*  itself is sound and isolates FENCE-as-ARBNO-body-prefix as the ingredient.
        expr  = LEN(1) ARBNO('+' LEN(1))
        '1+2+3' POS(0) expr RPOS(0)                     :S(Y)F(N)
Y OUTPUT = 'match'                                      :(END)
N OUTPUT = 'nomatch'
END
